# Task 4 Project

## Task

The task description is available at https://drive.google.com/file/d/15jVnBPXaZrjs99KOUxp4TGq6Inau6xq_/view

## How to run the app

1. Install the required dependencies:

   npm install

2. Build the application (if needed):

   npm run build

3. Start the application in development mode:

   npm start

## Folder Structure and configuration

- `husky/` — configuration for Git hooks.
- `public/` — static files (HTML, images, etc.).
- `src/` — source code of the application (styles, logic).
- `tests/` — test files for checking functionality.
- `node_modules/` — installed Node.js packages.
- `package.json` — project metadata and dependencies.
- `webpack.config.js` — configuration for Webpack bundler.
- `prettierrc` — configuration for Prettier code formatter.
- `eslint.config.js` — configuration for ESLint linter.
- `jest.config.js` — configuration for Jest testing framework.
